[0.202, "o", "[2/4] PowerDNS deployment running in the kind cluster.\r\n[3/4] Local API port-forward ready at http://127.0.0.1:18081 (header: X-API-Key: pdns4kube-dev-key)\r\nHandling connection for 1053\r\n      Local DNS port-forward ready at 127.0.0.1:1053 (try: dig +tcp @127.0.0.1 -p 1053 example.org NS)\r\n[4/4] Launching operator locally (press Ctrl+C to stop)..."]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[1;35r\u001b[1;1H\u001b[11S\u001b[12BOperator running locally.\u001b[15;1H------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\nTry it manually (copy-paste while the operator is running):\u001b[18;1H1. Create a DNSZone for example.org with two NS records:\u001b[20;1Hkubectl apply -f demo/dnszone.yaml\u001b[22;1H2. Update it (switch the NS records to ns3/ns4):\u001b[24;1Hkubectl apply -f demo/dnszone-updated.yaml\r\n\u001b[K\r\n3. Verify in Kubernetes and in PowerDNS:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\nkubectl get dnszones\u001b[K\r\ndig +tcp @127.0.0.1 -p 1053 example.org NS\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n4. Remove it when done:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\nkubectl delete dnszone example-org\u001b[K\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[1;36r\u001b[35;1H\u001b[?2026l"]
